duties:
 - Teach a minimum of 36 hours; 

2 - Prepare teaching resources for each class and provide relevant materials; 

3 - Assess and evaluate students' work and provide a final course grade according to OISE/UT grading practices; 

4 - Be available for informal meetings/communications with students as necessary.

qualifications_minimum:
1-Candidate must be working towards a doctoral degree in psychology or related field; 

2-Expertise in content area;  

3-Experience conducting and/or knowledge of play research and implementation of play in educational settings; 

4- Prior experience teaching graduate courses preferred.

tutorial:
Lectures: Mondays 13:00-15:00;
Tutorials: Mondays 15:00-16:00, Tuesdays 12:00-13:00;
Attendance at the lectures and tutorials is required. The lectures and tutorials are published in the Arts & Science timetable and cannot be changed.
